-- WI-754 (review follow-ups): TOP-LEVEL predicates for two cases the head-only
-- functor check cannot classify on its own, so the CLI resolves first and, for an
-- empty result, consults the discrimination index before refusing.
--   * an arity-0 PROPOSITION sits in no functor-enumeration table (it matches
--     only through the discrim tree), so a FALSE one resolves empty yet is
--     declared — it must read `no solutions`, not "unknown functor";
--   * a bounded QUANTIFIER (`forall_in` / `some_in`) is a resolver special form
--     with no rule/fact, recognised by short name.
fact base(1)
fact base(2)
rule holds :- base(1)       -- proposition, TRUE
rule never :- base(999)     -- proposition, FALSE — base(999) is absent
